The viridis, magma and inferno colour maps are by Stéfan van der Walt and Nathaniel J. Smith, released to the public
domain (CC0); their 256-entry tables were exported from matplotlib.

Filter design, window definitions and spectral scaling follow the published conventions of SciPy
(BSD-3-Clause, https://scipy.org) so that results can be compared with it; no SciPy code is included. SciPy, NumPy and
mpmath are used only to generate the test references in reference/ and tests/fixtures/.

The example data in examples/ are synthetic and were generated by reference/generate_fixtures.py.
